# TASK-260715-2btjwm reviewer verdict

## Verdict

Changes requested. Route to development.

## Blocking finding

The macOS-only generated workspace emits ReluxProxyIOS.xcscheme and ReluxProxyIOSTunnel.xcscheme, and xcodebuild -workspace ReluxTunnel.xcworkspace -list exposes both schemes. Project.swift creates both as shared schemes with hidden=true, but the accepted architecture ADR lines 157-158 requires them to be defined and disabled/not generated in macOS-only mode. The isShown=false state is written only to generated xcuserdata/xcschememanagement.plist, which is ignored, user-specific state; it does not prevent CI command-line discovery or invocation. The validator currently requires exactly eight Xcode-visible schemes, so it enforces the mismatch.

Required rework: keep the deferred iOS scheme names as source-controlled future inputs, but do not emit them in the macOS-only generated graph. Update validation to require exactly the six active macOS/package/relay schemes and explicitly reject the two deferred iOS schemes from xcodebuild output. Document how the later iOS-resume input enables them.

